      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      We can restate condition $(2)$ as follows: each fiber $\calX ^{/U}$ of $p$ is presentable, and each of the pullback functors $f^{\ast }: \calX ^{/V} \rightarrow \calX ^{/U}$ preserves small colimits. It is clear that $(1) \Rightarrow (2)$, and that $(2)$ implies that colimits in $\calX $ are universal. Since $\calX $ admits finite limits, it has a final object $1$; condition $(2)$ implies that $\calX \simeq \calX ^{/1}$ is presentable, which proves $(1)$. 
